 ### Added
 
 - `./css`: `collectAnimationOptions` keeps the author's time unit: each `CSSAnimationOptions` row gains `durationUnit` / `delayUnit` (`CssTimeUnit`, `"s" | "ms"`, lowercased; css-values-4 §7.3) beside a `duration` / `delay` read from a number, so a consumer can write `250ms` and `0.25s` back as authored (X.KF.W13X `.r3res2f`, UIA-KF-177). `duration` and `delay` are unchanged, still in seconds.
+- `./color`: `parseCssColor` and `serializeCssColor` (with the types they name: `CssColor`, `CssColorSpace`, `ParseResult`, `ParseIssue`) are published here too, so a page that only reads and writes colours never loads the value and stylesheet grammar (X-W12U `.g2s`). `parseCssColor` now runs on a `<color>`-rooted parser: the same BBNF grammar, `src/css/grammar/color.bbnf` compiled as a root of its own (entry `colorTop`, `src/css/bbnf/generated/color.js`). They are the same functions `./css` exports, which is unchanged; a colour-only bundle drops from the whole `./css` grammar (35,830 B gz) to the colour grammar alone.
 
